  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Intensified Malaria Control Project, Phase II (IMCP-II) - India (01-Oct-2015-31-Dec-2017)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">India, Malaria, Department of Economic Affairs, Ministry of Finance of India (DEA-M)This program has the following goals: To reduce malaria related morbidity by at least 50% and mortality by at least 50% in project areas (08 states) by 2017 as compared to 2012.. The objectives of this program are: To achieve 100% coverage in project areas by appropriate BCC activities to improve knowledge, awareness and responsive behaviour regarding effective preventive and curative malaria control interventions by 2017.  To achieve near universal coverage (80%) by 2017 by effective preventive intervention (LLIN) for population living in high risk project areas (API&gt;1).  To achieve universal coverage (100%) of fever cases by correct, affordable and appropriate parasitological diagnosis and prompt, effective treatment according to the national drug policy in project areas by 2017.  To strengthen health systems, community systems through capacity building (training) to improve service delivery in project areas by 2017.  To strengthen surveillance and M&amp;E, program planning and management, and coordination and partnership development to improve service delivery in project areas by 2017</narrative>
  </description>
